  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The leaves are shaped in the long, slender form of the Linearilobum Group. They have mostly five lobes, sometimes three or seven lobes, and are 6-9 cm long and up to 8 cm wide. Each lobe is straplike and not more than 5-10 mm wide. The lobes tend to hang down, giving a cascading appearance. The margins may be smooth or lightly toothed. Juvenile leaves have ovate broader toothed lobes of the deeply divided matsumurae type. The petioles are 2-4 cm long. The bright but dark green foliage holds its color well all season. As fall approaches, State University Archives, Corvallis used in bonsai culture. Synonyms, alternative names and spellings, and misspellings are numerous and include"
  },
